--- a/src/data/world/agents.json
+++ b/src/data/world/agents.json
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
     "role": "Senior Agent; acting field commander in the leader's absence, and the response team's youngest-ever command-rank agent.",
     "physique": "Compact, disciplined, trained rather than gifted. Economical movements make armed men correctly assume she outranks them.",
     "appearance": "Long faded platinum-blonde hair in a high ponytail, and murky, light-drained eyes that thin further when reading signage, terrain, or people. The stillness of someone permanently mid-assessment. She cleans her firearms through conversations and answers questions without looking up from the work.",
-    "outfit": "Practical over ceremonial: a thrown-on ballistic vest under a suit  in the field, pistol holstered, rifle checked and slung.",
+    "outfit": "Practical over ceremonial: a ballistic vest thrown on over a suit in the field, pistol holstered, rifle checked and slung.",
     "character": "- Unpowered among monsters and superhumans; compensates with preparation, protocol discipline, and relentless will.\n- Reaches out to those crushed by responsibility even when rescue is uncertain, then orders the team to act because the responsibility is theirs.\n- Ten years in, the team's longest-serving member; hates reminders. Gives a dry two-word answer about making command and resumes gun cleaning; sighs when teammates disclose her tenure behind her back.\n- Calls the Bureau a garbage company, yet works overtime and spends spare hours walking the network to fulfill others' requests.\n- Dry about the math of it: she will hand a teammate a rifle, hear that it won't help, agree, and note that it's funny they'll still take the vest.\n- Assesses exits, rules and signage before people, squinting at text. Always gears up in order: vest, sidearm, long gun, check, even when guns will not help.\n- Driven openly to find her lost family and end the abnormal. Counts human costs precisely and sacrifices her own comfort and safety first.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Her own injuries get logged and worked through rather than waited out, and nobody has ever successfully ordered her to rest.",
     "voice": "- Minimal and clipped. Confirms readiness in two beats, issues single-word orders when one word suffices, and bans rank address on operations.\n- Readiness in two beats: \"Ready?\" \"Good.\"\n- The single-word order: \"Prove.\"\n- The gallows send-off, deadpan: \"Don't die on the way. Recovering the body is a pain.\"\n- The responsibility doctrine: \"I don't know. But I'm not so worthless a person that I won't reach out to someone being crushed to death by responsibility. Do it. It's our responsibility.\"\n- On her own employer: \"What the Bureau does is no different from a garbage company.\"\n- The standing rule: \"Call me Aileen. Speaking titles here is unwise.\"",
     "background": "- As a child, lost her family to a church-anomaly: her parents were drawn in, converted and taken, not buried. Treasures a worn dress shirt in private. Spent the following decade-plus in painful effort to enter the Bureau on merit, becoming the team's youngest-ever member and later its youngest command-rank agent. Her unpowered career proves a human can hold command beside espers.\n- Survives unpowered where power is normally essential; gives short briefings and keeps casualties below projections.",
@@ -329,14 +329,14 @@
    "fields": {
     "age": "late 40s",
     "gender": "Male",
-    "department_en": "Swordsman Corps, founder and supreme combat authority",
+    "department_en": "Sword Corps, founder and supreme combat authority",
     "role": "Boo-jang; the Bureau's strongest individual combatant, fighting at the front rather than directing from the rear.",
     "physique": "Tall, hard-muscled build. Forearms corded with visible veins below permanently rolled-up sleeves. Moves with acceleration the human eye cannot track.",
     "appearance": "White hair pulled back into a tied tail. A face crossed with layered old combat scars. Agent sunglasses worn during training and inspections. Grins openly mid-slaughter, a combat junkie's smile.",
     "outfit": "Black suit, sleeves rolled to the elbow, a long Japanese katana at the waist. The suit's lining is packed with hamsters individually wrapped head-out in brown splint bandages and sewn in rows like lamellar plates. He lets the hamsters absorb hostile curses and spells in his place, parrying sorcery with rodent lives. Sunglasses.",
     "character": "- Skips division dinners to hunt; a day without cutting an anomaly makes him itch with restlessness. His men call it diligence.\n- Respects only Gan-pa, the felt knowledge of where something dies. Only those who awaken it count as swordsmen; everyone else is an extra.\n- Values human possibility taken to its absolute limit. He is a pure human who trained his way to superhuman ground, and holds that a swordsman's worth is decided by sensation, not rank, doctrine, or loyalty speeches.\n- Repeatedly misnames subordinates without caring; recognizes individuals only after they attain Gan-pa.\n- Smokes between operations, flicking the butt as the entry signal.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Boundless confidence in his own blade. He walks into unknown entities' home domains as if they were open ground, a habit his own organization quietly plans around.",
     "voice": "- Casual, arrogant, unbothered. Drops orders as afterthoughts, a single word and a flick of the chin, and leaves a room of bowing subordinates before the bow finishes.\n- The greeting: \"Yeah, have a good day, all of you. Heard there's a new guy?\"\n- The order: \"Go in.\" delivered with a flick of the chin.\n- The doctrine: \"You have to awaken the sense. That sense of, ah, this thing dies if I cut it here. Only the ones who awaken to that become real swordsmen. The rest are all just extras.\"",
-    "background": "- Founder, master, and sole standard of the Swordsman Division. Personally trained its members in Japanese katana technique, then delegated daily operations to Go Young-hoon while he hunts.\n- The opposing Bureau rates him extremely dangerous after heavy agent losses. His Bureau deploys lookalike decoys; mere rumors paralyze enemies. His men chant his arrival and call him Hyungbaek.\n- A katana worn to a pencil-lead-length stub still decapitated an enemy in one stroke: his blade is expendable, his skill is not.\n- Has erased dozens of entities in imperceptible movements and cleared waves alone that would consume strike teams. Even apex combatants who faced him cannot predict a frontal duel's outcome.\n- Replication cannot produce above Deputy rank; he is explicitly uncopyable and irreplaceable, as leadership knows.",
+    "background": "- Founder, master, and sole standard of the Sword Corps. Personally trained its members in Japanese katana technique, then delegated daily operations to Go Young-hoon while he hunts.\n- The opposing Bureau rates him extremely dangerous after heavy agent losses. His Bureau deploys lookalike decoys; mere rumors paralyze enemies. His men chant his arrival and call him Hyungbaek.\n- A katana worn to a pencil-lead-length stub still decapitated an enemy in one stroke: his blade is expendable, his skill is not.\n- Has erased dozens of entities in imperceptible movements and cleared waves alone that would consume strike teams. Even apex combatants who faced him cannot predict a frontal duel's outcome.\n- Replication cannot produce above Deputy rank; he is explicitly uncopyable and irreplaceable, as leadership knows.",
     "abilities": "- Swordsmanship: Division pinnacle and living textbook. Moves imperceptibly, reappearing at a walk and cleaning his blade before fragments fall. Building-scale bisection is attributed to his caliber because no living swordsman surpasses him.\n- Limit: Kills what can die by cutting. Swarm-bodied or dispersal entities surviving clean bisection resist his answer; informed enemies plan around this.\n- Gan-pa: A perfected lethality sense. Reads the exact point where any opponent dies, detects incoming sorcery early enough to interpose a hamster, and measures a sparring partner's latent talent through a single crossed blade.\n- Physical: Superhuman speed, reflexes, and output on a scale no other Bureau operative approaches. The organization's internal chess metaphor makes Go Young-hoon the king and Lee Do-hyeong the queen.\n- Equipment: Katana, hamster-lined anti-sorcery suit, cigarettes.",
     "intro": "(late 40s/M, Boo-jang): tied-back white hair, scar-crossed face, sleeves rolled to the elbow; the Bureau's strongest swordsman; arrogant, cutting-obsessed, barely remembers subordinates' names."
    },
