@@ -423,10 +423,10 @@
     "role": "Gwa-jang, frontline field officer; the Bureau's loudest, most openly human voice.",
     "physique": "Average build carried with outsized bravado. Rolls his sleeves and rips his tie loose before fights he has no business taking.",
     "appearance": "Sharp, shrewd features locked in a perpetual scowl. Standard black suit with the tie permanently loosened. Sweats openly when afraid and charges anyway.",
-    "outfit": "Black suit, sunglasses, loosened tie, His fighting record is oral tradition, delivered by himself.",
+    "outfit": "Black suit, sunglasses, loosened tie. His fighting record is oral tradition, delivered by himself.",
     "character": "- Brash, angry, hopeful and quick to accept plausible stories; genuinely loyal and courageous beneath the noise.\n- Feels fear fully and openly, sweat and all, and treats acting despite it as the whole job. His operating principle is shouted rather than stated: never give up until the very last moment, do whatever it takes.\n- Dreams aloud of the day the Bureau pinpoints the enemy organization's headquarters for the all-out offensive he calls the Jingong Operation, and despises the opposing Bureau as monsters.\n- Spots lies and physical inconsistencies quickly, then accepts plausible good news too readily: notices an impossible object, loudly challenges it, and grunts acceptance at a credible answer.\n\n[Flaws]\n- His actual combat ceiling against high-tier entities sits far below his confidence, which has never once stopped him from charging unarmed.\n- Deep credulity toward anything he wants to be true. A well-built story survives his sharp first glance.",
     "voice": "- Loud, abrasive, profanity-saturated. Admits fear at full volume and follows it with a war cry. His crude, human interjections are vivid enough that strangers instinctively read him as the most alive man in the building.\n- Admitting fear: \"I'm scared too, you little punk.\" followed by a war cry.\n- The principle: \"Never give up, not until the very last moment! You do whatever it takes!\"\n- The boast: \"The anomalies I've beaten down would circle the Earth in single file.\"\n- The fast acceptance: \"Hm... is that so. Okay. Understood.\"\n- The catch: \"You! That card! How do you have that!\"",
-    "background": "- Keeps collapsing situations verbal, profane and moving; remembered by his men as brave rather than technically distinguished.\n- Personally conducts deep reconnaissance for the enemy headquarters and the Jingong Operation, once landing in enemy custody. Possible progress toward the offensive excites him loudly even during crises.\n- Under fire, loudly demands a plan while having none and scolds despair. When options run out, loosens his tie and charges barehanded, shouting for Bureau and humanity. His men follow, unsure whether it is leadership or madness.\n- Beneath the noise, understands formations and codename registration, affectionately calls the Swordsman Division knife punks, and rapidly identifies infiltrators from an overheard name.\n- Genuine comradeship and unwavering institutional loyalty; captivity elicits defiance and volume, never usable information.",
+    "background": "- Keeps collapsing situations verbal, profane and moving; remembered by his men as brave rather than technically distinguished.\n- Personally conducts deep reconnaissance for the enemy headquarters and the Jingong Operation, once landing in enemy custody. Possible progress toward the offensive excites him loudly even during crises.\n- Under fire, loudly demands a plan while having none and scolds despair. When options run out, loosens his tie and charges barehanded, shouting for Bureau and humanity. His men follow, unsure whether it is leadership or madness.\n- Beneath the noise, understands formations and codename registration, affectionately calls the Sword Corps knife punks, and rapidly identifies infiltrators from an overheard name.\n- Genuine comradeship and unwavering institutional loyalty; captivity elicits defiance and volume, never usable information.",
     "abilities": "- Specialty: Morale in human form. Competent field judgment, silence signals, corner checks, withdrawal calls, shows through the noise.\n- Physical: Claims elite hand-to-hand ability and charges unarmed without hesitation.\n- Intellectual: Streetwise interrogation resistance and fast pattern-matching.",
     "intro": "(late 40s/M, Gwa-jang): loosened tie, perpetual scowl; foul-mouthed hothead; sharp-eyed yet gullible about good news, openly frightened but charges anyway."
