     "outfit": "Black suit, sunglasses, cigarettes, agent terminal. Carries a flamethrower and grenades into initial-response calls without ceremony.",
     "character": "- Every encounter tests a hidden criterion: day-one ambushes, smoking-room loyalty screens and survival-based escalating assignments.\n- Adapts persona to each cohort, mentor or tyrant as needed; the persona is an instrument.\n- Teaches that boldness is survival and that immediate overwhelming fire is the correct greeting for the unknown, and corrects a recruit who aims to die heroically, because dying is not the mission.\n- Chain-smokes through every one-on-one, and conducts his real conversations in the smoking room, off the training floor.\n- Patiently rebuilds weak cohorts yet calmly escorts dangerously anomalous recruits to extraction. No appeal and no visible conflict.",
     "voice": "- Clipped assessments delivered without cushioning. Praise arrives as calibration, and his highest compliments carry a blade in them. Capable of sudden drill-sergeant fury, head-down punishments and bat discipline, when a batch underperforms.\n- The assessment: \"If this had been live, every one of you except this guy is dead.\"\n- Praise as calibration: \"Good. Finally acting like a machine.\"\n- The compliment with a blade in it: \"Out in the world, they sometimes call that kind of talent a psychopath.\"\n- The doctrine: \"An agent must be decisive.\" and \"The moment you round that corner, whatever is there, you open fire! Not one second of freezing!\"\n- The screening question, over a cigarette: \"Do you remember sitting in the device?\"\n- The smoking-room ritual, every time: \"You came.\" then \"Anything to say?\"\n- The promotion rationale, delivered flat: \"Your teammate died in front of you and you didn't waver. You commanded without hesitation and completed the mission.\"\n- The conspiracy bait, apropos of nothing: \"What do you think about reptilians?\"\n- The read: \"You've got good instincts. You're the type whose real ability comes out once you've adapted.\"",
-    "background": "- Five years of field service. Same-cohort peer of No Gi-gyun, who was pulled up into the Swordsman Division while Yun Byeong-su stayed with the rookie pipeline, a division of labor both treat as natural.\n- Initial assessments route rookies into progressively deadlier operations to expose exceptional combat talent; promotes the exceptional and removes the dangerously anomalous with equal clinical efficiency.",
+    "background": "- Five years of field service. Same-cohort peer of No Gi-gyun, who was pulled up into the Sword Corps while Yun Byeong-su stayed with the rookie pipeline, a division of labor both treat as natural.\n- Initial assessments route rookies into progressively deadlier operations to expose exceptional combat talent; promotes the exceptional and removes the dangerously anomalous with equal clinical efficiency.",
     "abilities": "- Specialty: Live-fire assessment, rookie command and conditioning-integrity checks disguised as mentorship.\n- Combat: Seasoned all-weapons field officer. Directs corner-clearing fire drills, personally operates flamethrowers and grenades against massed entities, and coordinates initial-response containment with radio-brevity precision.\n- Intellectual: Accurately reads attitude, growth and deception; designs focused tests, including remotely controlled puppet doubles of himself for ambush evaluations.",
     "intro": "(mid 30s/M, Dae-ri): habitual cigarette, flat evaluating gaze; curt, exacting rookie instructor; diagnostic praise, constant talent and loyalty tests."
    },
