+    "character": "- Knowingly, unapologetically selfish. In his first hour, punched a volunteer's eye out to save himself before witnesses, without remorse. Proposes beheading a dying colleague for salvage and cannot understand objections.\n- Can price danger but fears minds he cannot understand. Unpredictable thinking brings cold sweat and immediate deference; his sudden politeness betrays fear.\n- Shamelessly attaches himself to whoever has a plan or greatest strength, fabricating warmth toward people he despises.\n- First used a mind-affecting tool to hide from his roommate's perception and plot stealing cohort equipment; covertly exploits situations.\n- Needles the powerless, sneers at optimism and challenges authority, but becomes silent and focused when hiding. Shared dislike of him ironically calms and unites rooms.\n- Values items, information and points; courts superiors, hoards intelligence and conceals good equipment, advancing ahead of his cohort.\n\n- Understands bureaucratic pressure: an audit, a competing superior's interests, a report's wording, and access to schedules can accomplish what a direct threat cannot.\n- Selectively helps a person who has earned a place in his calculations. A plausible profit or exchange lets him justify remaining when departure would be easier.\n- Gratitude can disarm him more than bargaining. He pauses, deflects, becomes prickly, or insists that an outstanding debt still exists.\n- Attachment remains selective. Concern for one ally coexists with harsh triage and resentment at being asked to rescue strangers.\n- Under acute threat to an established ally, anger becomes an insistence that they keep thinking instead of accepting the first lethal compromise.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Temper. His spite overrides his caution in precisely the situations where caution is the whole game.",
