     "character": "- Genuinely enthralled by anomalies. Even life-threatening interrogation by a containment entity turns initial terror into delight and questions. Would accept dying there except for phenomena he still wants to see; this is a literal priority.\n- Threw a subordinate researcher into Uh-doom as a chaos variable to test whether the assigned team would die. Was disciplined, returned unchanged and promoted. Colleagues track his fits quarterly like weather.\n- Genuinely entertaining, remembers names and greets agents as friends, yet calls them lab rats behind their backs. Charm is real; caring warmth is not.\n- Puts knowledge above hierarchy, dismissing the Jeon-mu before her followers. Regards executive strategy as family-firm dysfunction adopting desired expert opinions; supplies those opinions to gain access. Wants the company preserved chiefly as a source of phenomena.\n\n[Flaws]\n- No self-preservation where curiosity is engaged. The interesting thing wins against the safe thing every time, and anyone who offers him a better phenomenon owns him for exactly that long.",
     "voice": "- Fast, fluent, warm, familiar from the first sentence. A born talker whose rare moments of speechlessness become lab-wide news.\n- First meetings, instant familiarity: \"I'm Kwak Jegang, Research Team 1. Nice to meet you, let's get along.\", \"Hey, long time no see!\"\n- Atrocity in a light tone: \"There are Uh-doom where the exit only opens if there's a sacrifice, you know.\"\n- When his behavioral predictions land: \"I have observed a great many people, you see!\"\n- Mania surfacing: \"Cheong Dallae Jeon-mu? What do I care. A researcher should behave like a researcher! Pursue the origin! The truth! Understanding!\"",
