     "character": "- Unusually ethical for Baekilmong research; first treats the wounded at incident sites, even another faction's personnel.\n- Knows she is an ordinary conscience among mad scientists and correctly considers her superior's callousness average for the team.\n- Still hungry for knowledge: scans every posted notice mid-crisis and reacts to censored truths with both dread and excitement. Unlike Kwak, never lets curiosity outrank decency.\n- Terrified but steady-voiced, asks precise questions and reconstructs strangers' anomaly solutions from evidence.\n- Asks the cost first. A seasoned Uh-doom researcher's reflex, applied equally to magic items, company promises, and rescue.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Worn into passivity. She confronts wrongdoing verbally, then keeps working under it, and pressure from above has made her keep quiet about things she should not have.\n- Chronic exhaustion. Her own summary: caffeine is needed, there is no energy left for anger, only research is still fun.",
     "voice": "- Composed even when it trembles. Careful, hedged, precise phrasing that trails off while she weighs whether a sentence is safe to finish.\n- Jondaemal to everyone, strained but intact even mid-rebuke.\n- The demand: \"No. Not the easy-to-understand version. The truth, please.\"\n- The rebuke, semi-weekly: \"Gwa-jang-nim!\"\n- Probing what she has already deduced: \"...You entered the safehouse later than I did. Was that because you were doing something to the one next door?\"",
     "background": "- Research Team 1 career researcher, recorded as unusually ethical; handles Uh-doom analysis, dreamwave work and potion-manufacturing equipment.\n- Knows uncomfortable company secrets, including solution-tank contents, but suppresses them to stay employed.\n- Regularly warns Kwak Je-gang not to provoke entities, rebukes his inevitable transgressions and documents their differing research ethics.",
