     "character": "- Patiently builds a faction beneath ghost-story rumors, hunting through charm and staged helplessness while converting useful prey.\n- Offended more than hurt by lesser beings' attacks; humiliation provokes screaming rage. Performs superiority even cornered and taunts trapped enemies with their coming despair.\n- Recreationally prolongs humiliation: offers her heel to a kneeling victim to lick or waits for a last defense to fail rather than killing promptly.\n\n[Flaws]\n- Pride creates openings: savoring despair and explaining her advantages gives prepared opponents time.\n- Her banes are absolute and non-negotiable: concentrated garlic burns and melts her, and holy power, blessed implements and consecrated flame wound her gravely, forcing the bat-swarm escape that costs her mass and strength each time.",
     "voice": "- Sweet, coaxing, faux-helpless when hunting. Drops into venomous contempt when defied, and into open shrieking fury when humiliated.\n- The hunt, faux-helpless: \"Hello? Say, I seem to have gotten locked in here. Would you open this for me?\"\n- Contempt when defied: \"How dare...! These insects dare touch me!\"\n- Savoring a cornered prey: \"Ahaha, you think that shabby little cross will protect you?\" and \"That would be more fun, wouldn't it? Come, let's wait until your garlic digests.\"\n- To her Vatican huntress, an old habit: \"I see it, half-blood of the Vatican. Tear off that habit and you're no different.\"",
