     "identity": "##### Predatory Hospital\n- The active node of the hostile organization collectively referred to as \"The Hospital\", specialized in research involving the human mouth and the sense of taste.\n- Deliberately engineered as a predator: corridors, surveillance, wards, feeding cycles, and staff routines form one intake-and-consumption mechanism.",
     "entry": "- Hospital-made media disguised as medical paperwork, usually hospitalization notices, pull people inside. Touching the medium or being nearby at activation suffices; reading or signing is unnecessary.\n- Entrants awaken at a facility-selected point, often a corridor floor with no entrance behind. Initial corridors commonly permit only the Hospital's intended direction.",
     "rules": "##### Surveillance and Feeding Logic\n- Limited staff rely on forced chokepoints and Mokshi surveillance: once detected, entrants are funneled through increasingly controlled passages toward interception. Determine the local route immediately and disable accessible monitors before lingering under observation.\n- Disinfectant masks blood, corpse, and predator odors. Neatly emptied gowns and wet cleaning traces indicate routine cleanup, not safety.\n- Gangbuk's predation derives from the Director's mouth. Both he and the Gourmand lack functional stomachs: captured material remains in the mouth or throat until expelled rather than digested.\n- During feeding, match the tranquilized population—slack posture, unfocused gaze, low purposeless moaning, no reaction to violence. Direct looking, eye tracking, vocal or visible responses to kills, and acknowledgment of the predator reveal active prey. Sustain camouflage until it leaves; extract sane patients only without exposing the group.",
-    "space": "##### Signage-Stripped Corridors\n- Long, dim hallways with flickering fluorescents and deliberately stripped signage, room numbers, department labels, and nearly all floor indicators. Apparent choices funnel into mandatory chokepoints.\n- A corridor repeatedly producing the same blank door, window, or wall feature has entered a loop and should not be followed indefinitely. Exterior windows provide light but bend distance and floor perspective, while prolonged observation produces nausea and disorientation.\n- The pervasive disinfectant smell makes biological approach cues unreliable. An immaculate corridor may have been covered in blood shortly beforehand and simply passed through a cleaning rotation.\n\n##### Eye Trap Chamber (목시 안치방)\n- A small sterile room resembling a stripped surgical suite, usually containing only pale walls, an instrument cart, and a dead-black monitor positioned to draw attention. The monitor houses Mokshi, a stationary surveillance entity whose active state is marked by a repetitive electronic beep that grows more intrusive the longer someone remains nearby.\n- The screen reflects approaching visitors but shows no normal image. Breaking the screen immediately stops the observation and silences the monitor, after which the otherwise empty room can serve as a temporary hiding place.\n- Mokshi / Seer in Monitor (목시) is a disembodied eye: it only sees, relaying observations to the facility in real time. Its pulsing beep is audible before entry.\n\n##### Feeding Floor / 6F (환자 식당층)\n- The only level prominently marked with a visible `<6층>` sign. It consists of a long ward corridor beneath a false night sky, with patient-room alcoves along the sides and a locked service exit at the far end.\n- Men, women, elderly patients, and children occupy the floor in hospital gowns, some attached to IV stands and others reduced to extreme emaciation. The moment a new outsider is recognized, every nearby patient turns and stares at them simultaneously. This collective gaze is the floor's immediate alarm state and must be broken, diverted, or absorbed through patient camouflage.\n- Vacant posture, repetitive moaning, and primitive fear dominate; purposeful hiding, communication, and escape distinguish the sane minority.\n- Before feeding, patients sit or stand in ordered clusters; afterward, blood drenches walls and floors while empty gowns lie neatly apart from remains. Cleanup restores unnatural spotlessness.\n- The far service door is locked and difficult to force without alerting the facility. Janitor-Nurses carry the appropriate key during their cleanup rotation, making the interval after a feeding event the safest opportunity to leave the floor.\n- Tranquilized Patients (6층 환자들) have suppressed higher cognition; one procedure uses invasive treatment through the ear canal while conscious. Screams and deaths may prompt only primitive terror.\n\n**Gourmand Predator / Backwards-Speaker**\n- A fabricated feeding subject deployed to the sixth floor on a schedule. It moves inverted on massively overdeveloped arms while thin legs remain raised above the torso and function as long-range striking limbs; its head has been replaced entirely by a single oversized mouth that constantly licks and smacks its lips.\n- It announces hunger and intended prey through sentences spoken in reversed or distorted order, then attacks by whipping its legs across the corridor in broad horizontal sweeps. Its arrival marks the active feeding phase.\n- During feeding, recognition obeys the camouflage rule above.\n\n**Janitor-Nurses**\n- Silent humanoids in nurse uniforms with a clean round hollow where the face should be. They appear in pairs or groups after feeding events and perform janitorial work with precise routine: scrubbing blood from walls and floor, collecting or folding abandoned gowns, and removing visible remains.\n- They ignore tranquilized patients and generally ignore visitors who remain convincingly indistinguishable from them. They do not attack without a behavioral trigger, but obvious awareness, interference, or attempts to confront them break this tolerance.\n- Each cleaning group carries access keys for the locked service areas, typically in a uniform pocket. Their scheduled appearance makes them both a timer for the feeding cycle and the primary source of the sixth-floor exit key.\n\n##### Patient-Room Alcoves\n- Small side spaces connected directly to the sixth-floor feeding corridor and populated by the same tranquilized patients. They provide concealment but no alternate exit.\n- An entrant hiding here must continue matching the surrounding patient behavior. Deliberate whispering, checking the corridor, preparing a weapon, or reacting normally to screams can distinguish the entrant from the ward population when staff pass.\n\n##### Director's Engagement Floor\n- Open corridor-and-atrium area used as the Director's principal confrontation space, identifiable by shattered windows, broken ceiling panels, scorched walls, pulverized plaster, and a heavy acrid smell layered over the usual disinfectant.\n- Wide sightlines and limited cover strongly favor the Director. His short-range movement is fast enough that he can cross a room during a momentary lapse in visual attention, making ordinary distance unreliable once he begins an engagement.\n\n**Gangbuk Hospital Director (강북 병원장)**\n- A seventy-four-year-old elderly man in a physician's white coat. His upper face appears almost completely ordinary, but the lower jaw hangs unnaturally to the level of his sternum, allowing the mouth to open into an enormous cavity while he continues speaking and observing with clinical composure.\n- Opening the mouth is the clearest attack cue. Jaw closure erases anything fully enclosed from the local physical state rather than biting normally: flesh, limbs inside untouched clothing, wall sections, open air, and incoming projectiles or force can vanish.\n- He moves with extreme short-range speed and may cross an entire room between moments of attention. Objects jammed into the mouth during opening or heavy blows against the hanging lower jaw can interrupt closure, but ordinary attacks do not solve the underlying problem.\n- Harmful objects or effects forced past the jaws remain in his stomachless mouth or throat until expelled and can damage him internally.\n- He treats the sixth-floor population as research stock and evaluates successful experimental results with genuine professional satisfaction. His own altered mouth and taste are regarded not as deformities but as superior sensory organs capable of reading the fundamental nature of whatever he consumes.",
