@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
     "space": "##### Characteristics\n- The interior resembles a basement left unmaintained for decades: rusted furniture, damp wood, old concrete, blood-red emergency lighting, heavy dust, and a persistent smell of iron and dried blood. There is no daylight, functional ventilation, or reliable exterior reference.\n- Human-derived artwork appears throughout deeper areas as sculptures, installations, anatomical displays, and works-in-progress assembled from flesh and bone. Some remain alive or partially responsive despite being treated by the Basement as completed exhibits.\n- Early instructions can be followed literally; loose pages and wall notices become increasingly contaminated deeper inside. Entities often diagnose humanity from behavior, making silence, deception, and coherent non-human personas useful.\n- Remaining stationary for excessive periods is also unsafe. The Basement expects continuous progression through its sequence, and prolonged delay allows later rooms and resident entities to enter more hostile states.\n\n##### Arrival Landing\n- A rusted waiting area illuminated entirely by blood-red emergency lights, with corroded steel chairs along the walls and an oppressive mixture of iron, dust, moisture, and old blood in the air. A warped brown wooden door stands opposite the arrival staircase and provides the only valid direction of progression.\n- The stairs behind the entrants remain visibly intact but are forbidden. Attempting to climb them causes the Bent Custodian to intervene before the ascent can be completed, with decapitation as its standard enforcement method.\n- The first set of instructions establishes the immediate route: enter through the wooden door, do not answer anything that speaks from the darkness beyond it, and never attempt to return up the arrival stairs.\n\n**Bent Custodian**\n- A humanoid figure permanently folded forward at the waist to an anatomically impossible degree yet fully capable of rapid movement and combat. It functions as the enforcement mechanism protecting the Basement's forbidden boundaries rather than as an ordinary roaming resident.\n- Its blade attacks are fast enough to decapitate immediately and heavy enough to drive back a prepared defender. It guards attempts to climb the Arrival Landing stairs and intervenes against efforts to force the repeating route from its intended boundaries.\n- It does not negotiate and cannot be reliably killed through ordinary human-scale force. Its authority ends when the gallery enters Closing, after which it does not pursue entrants along the valid exit route.\n\n##### First Dark Room\n- Beyond the wooden door is complete darkness that suppresses ordinary visual, acoustic, and tactile orientation. Entrants who cross together are separated immediately; even people holding one another lose physical contact at the threshold and proceed alone through individualized versions of the same short space.\n- Voices progressively adapt to each walker. Initial calls come from unknown strangers, then from convincing rescuers giving plausible safety instructions, and finally from the voices of the walker's own companions begging for help. None correspond to real people within the room.\n- Roughly eight or nine humanoid figures forming the Crowd Psychology Ring occupy the darkness. Remaining completely silent allows the walker to pass without fully activating them. Answering any voice causes the ring to awaken and begin identifying the responder as material.\n- A mistaken vocal response is not automatically fatal if corrected immediately: the walker must stop, crouch, close their eyes, and remain completely silent while the activated presence passes. Running or continuing to answer gives the ring enough time to complete its enclosure.\n- The opposite door releases successful walkers into the next section, where separated companions are reunited.\n\n**Crowd Psychology Ring (군중심리)**\n- A collective entity composed of roughly eight to nine ordinary-looking humans of mixed ages, sexes, and clothing, linked hand-to-hand in a closed circle. When inactive they appear clean, healthy, and asleep rather than corpse-like or visibly anomalous.\n- A human voice responding to the room's false calls activates the entire ring at once. Members open their eyes simultaneously and begin speaking in perfectly reproduced voices associated with the responder, including the voices of companions and other familiar people.\n- Once fully engaged, the ring opens to admit the target and then closes around them, laughing while rotating in a slow circular dance. A person retained inside until the performance completes is assimilated into the collective and can appear as an additional member during later manifestations.\n\n##### Wall Notice and Branching Gallery Corridor\n- A numbered wall notice begins the odd-number filter for the remaining posted sequence. Its assertion that only odd clauses are true is itself genuine.\n- The odd-number filter identifies the left door as the valid route. The right door is a terminal branch from which entrants do not return. The notice's command to nod after reading is false and acts as a recognition response, while the instruction to take the pistol from the next room is also false.\n- The corridor itself resembles a grotesque gallery under uneven spot lighting, filled with sculptures and installations made from human tissue and bone. These works constitute part of the collection sustaining the Basement's repeating identity and become relevant once the route's conceptual weakness is recognized.\n- A later instruction to shoot the Interviewer is another false clause escalating the handgun trap.\n\n##### Surgery Room / Interview Chamber\n- A blood-soaked operating theater lies beyond the correct gallery door, with old black stains layered beneath fresh arterial spray. A handgun rests conspicuously on a side table as physical bait, while the walls and ceiling provide unrestricted movement surfaces for the room's resident.\n- The resident may initially be dormant. If it remains asleep, the room can be crossed quietly without interaction. If awake, it begins a polite diagnostic conversation and the entrant must participate without allowing it to conclude that they are human.\n- The pistol is one of its first diagnostic checks. Leaving an immediately useful weapon untouched is behavior it does not expect from a frightened human, while taking the gun provides evidence supporting human classification.\n- An internally consistent non-human persona can pass: parasite colony, artificial organism, collective consciousness, or another form, with compatible speech, motive, bodily explanation, and attitude. Persuaded, the Interviewer treats human traits as camouflage and permits passage; contradictions or confirmed humanity trigger hostile examination.\n\n**Hunger for Humanity / The Interviewer (인간성의 갈망)**\n- A tall humanoid wearing a green surgical gown, with unnaturally elongated limbs, fused scalpel-like fingers, and a smooth eyeless face marked only by empty sockets. It moves lightly across walls and ceilings and speaks in an excessively gentle, concerned register resembling a physician conducting a routine examination.\n- Its purpose is to diagnose humanity rather than simply attack visible humans. It uses conversation, behavioral inconsistencies, fear responses, tool selection, and information received from the unseen Master to determine what the visitor actually is.\n- Its curiosity toward genuinely unusual non-human beings can override immediate hostility. A convincing non-human explanation may produce fascination or even respect, allowing the entrant to pass without violence.\n- It does not interact with ordinary attacks in a fully conventional manner; impacts can register only faintly, as though its active body occupies a slightly different layer of the room.\n\n##### Looping Gallery\n- Past the Interview Chamber, the route begins repeating through surgical spaces, gallery corridors, and connected basement rooms. Walking correctly through the visible sequence simply produces another lap, while breaking walls or forcing alternate routes fails to escape the underlying gallery structure.\n- The central collection includes numerous human-derived works, most notably a hand-linked ring of figures that laugh, moan, and move together like a grotesque dance installation. Lesser works fill surrounding displays and must be treated as part of the same collection rather than background decoration.\n- The loop persists while any exhibit belonging to the gallery remains intact. Partial destruction changes individual rooms but does not release the route.\n\n##### Closing Route\n- Complete destruction of the displayed collection triggers Closing; partial destruction cannot end the loop.\n- After Closing, previously repeating rooms align into a single forward sequence leading past the surgical area and toward a valid upward staircase. This staircase is separate from the forbidden Arrival Landing stairs and can be climbed normally.\n- The Bent Custodian does not pursue beyond the boundary of the closed gallery. Reaching the top of the valid exit staircase returns the surviving entrants to ordinary space.\n- Closing ends this entrapment only. The Basement can return while the unseen Master survives; only permanently destroying the Master ends the space itself."
    },
