decline.\n\n##### Maid\n- A female human cast member locked into the household Maid role. She retains basic human biology and can briefly communicate normally when the active scene permits it, but role pressure repeatedly pulls her behavior back into the production.\n- Her successful outcome is survival through the end of the performance rather than fulfillment of a special combat objective. Killing her as though she were an anomalous resident only removes a recoverable cast member.\n\n##### Recast Cast\n- Abducted humans whose roles overwrite prior identity with genuine warmth, history, and emotional certainty. Strangers sincerely know entrants as daughter, parent, sibling, employer, or another relation while forgetting their old selves. Keep them alive until the production ends; forced immediate recognition is not the recovery method.\n- These cast members function as hostages embedded into the script. Treating them as monsters or disposable extras strengthens the production's tragedy and permanently sacrifices people who could otherwise leave when the act resolves.\n\n##### Puppets / Puppet Swarm\n- The enforcement population of the act, created from dead cast members as well as additional bodies generated between scene turns. Converted dead retain recognizable appearance and costuming but lose meaningful independent reasoning.\n- Puppets move with jerky, string-driven articulation, bent necks, and occasional stuttering vocal fragments while possessing enough physical strength to break walls or kill ordinary humans with a single heavy strike. On open ground they can close distance with extreme speed.\n- Their numbers remain effectively renewable while the Stage Light continues operating, making systematic extermination an attrition trap rather than a valid ending condition.",
     "survival": "##### Resolution\n- Disable or seize the Stage Light as specified above; then prevent roles and scenes from rebuilding, protect surviving cast, and force the remaining performance toward resolution. Cross an end-of-act exit seam immediately before theatrical structure reasserts itself. Darkness does not remove existing Puppets or backstage attackers and makes them harder to track; coordinate and use sound."
