    "keys": "Bio-Assembly Factory, Bio-Factory, 생체 공장, 생체공장",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "- An active plant run by a hostile manufacturer under the Stationery Company parent brand: public retail stationery, novelty board games, and ordinary goods conceal anomalous-object manufacture and live-tissue human duplication.\n- Cheerful, family-friendly branding masks a culture treating human suffering as production input. Mundane-looking goods conceal weaponized secondary functions.\n- Retail and even the Bureau's anomalous-object rental program distribute the brand, sustaining infiltration far beyond the factory.",
-    "entry": "- Standard infiltration uses ordinary front-line hiring. Background scrutiny is minimal: extreme turnover is intentional production throughput.\n- Hiring, attrition, and death are manufacturing variables; failed or unsuitable workers become raw material rather than being dismissed.\n- First-day passage through the Suspended-Subject Gallery tests disgust. Visible reactions to live subjects transfer applicants from workers to production stock.\n- New hires who pass the threshold are assigned to physical assembly labor and paired into shared dormitory quarters without privacy partitioning. Direct supervision is handled by an automaton-class Foreman rather than a human middle manager, eliminating any human chain-of-command capable of softening factory procedures.",
+    "entry": "- Standard infiltration uses ordinary front-line hiring. Background scrutiny is minimal: extreme turnover is intentional production throughput.\n- Hiring, attrition, and death are manufacturing variables; failed or unsuitable workers become raw material rather than being dismissed.\n- First-day passage through the Suspended-Subject Gallery tests disgust. Visible reactions to live subjects transfer applicants from workers to production stock.\n- New hires who pass the threshold are assigned to physical assembly labor. Direct supervision is handled by an automaton-class Foreman rather than a human middle manager, eliminating any human chain-of-command capable of softening factory procedures.",
     "space": "##### Characteristics\n- Signs, contracts, manuals, and work instructions use warm phrasing such as \"thank you always for using our company's board games\" for ordinary goods and routine homicide, maiming, dismemberment, live-body handling, vivisection, and employee disposal alike.\n- The company does not voluntarily recall products after harm is established. Known recalls occur only after Bureau intervention.\n- All working areas carry a persistent smell of viscera, iron, and chemical reagents. Ventilation is deliberately poor, and continuous human screaming from suspended test subjects remains audible through shifts and breaks.\n- Known leaked products include a self-playing emotion-amplifier piano originally marketed as a mood-following instrument and recalled after becoming a suicide driver; a 1990s-vintage unlimited-flame butane canister that remains in active Bureau use as an anti-intruder ignition source; and the \"Love Board Game,\" a rental item that compels players to perform physical acts during play.\n\n##### Locations\n###### Factory Front Office\n- A clean corporate reception area used exclusively to intake new hires and presented as ordinary industrial HR processing. The Foreman personally greets arrivals and escorts them into the plant. The first-day tour follows a fixed winding route from reception through the Suspended-Subject Gallery, then the Residue Disposal Room, and finally the Main Assembly Line, deliberately exposing applicants to progressively stronger thresholds of disgust and compliance.\n\n###### Suspended-Subject Gallery\n- A long industrial hall filled with living human subjects suspended from overhead hook-and-rail hardware shaped like oversized coat hangers. The subjects remain conscious enough to vocalize and serve simultaneously as live-tissue stock and as the factory's first psychological screening mechanism for incoming staff.\n\n**Suspended Test Subjects**\n- Living humans suspended from the gallery rail system who retain pain perception and the ability to vocalize. By the time they are brought into the upper production process, most have been psychologically reduced to a near-infant state and no longer produce coherent speech.\n- Extraction does not restore them to baseline human condition. Removal from the system is lethal in nearly all documented cases, making conventional rescue attempts functionally non-recoverative.\n\n###### Residue Disposal Room\n- A side room where staff manually sweep uncategorized black residue produced by failed experiments. The material is visually opaque, produces no burn smell, and does not correspond to ordinary chemistry; the plant classifies it simply as \"parts.\" The room is staffed by suited office-tier workers who visibly dry-heave while cleaning but continue working without refusal, and the task is treated as routine maintenance rather than a special disposal assignment.\n\n###### Main Assembly Line\n- A factory-grade conveyor carrying human sub-components including arms, legs, torsos, and heads through successive assembly stations. Floor workers manually attach limbs and heads to torsos as standard shift labor, producing a living duplicate of a specific person as the finished product. Head attachment in particular produces audible screaming from the in-progress copy itself rather than from a separate victim.\n- The duplication key is kept within operator reach of the main line, not in a secured vault: the most exploitable structural weakness.\n\n**Assembled Human Products**\n- Finished Assembled Human Products are standing, mobile copies activated by the keyed component.\n- Downstream buyers use these products as \"people,\" and internal company language describes the market as continuously high-demand. The copies demonstrate genuine pain responses during assembly, while their post-assembly behavioral profile remains undetermined from available infiltration data.\n\n###### Shared Dormitory\n- An austere three-bed room assigned to new-hire teams regardless of sex, with a shared sink, a rudimentary kitchen fixture, and no privacy partitioning. It is the only designated rest environment inside the compound, causing psychological damage accumulated during the shift to continue and intensify overnight rather than being relieved.",
     "rules": "##### Labor and Production Control\n- Forced live-body processing makes most hires quit, collapse, or become raw material within one or two shifts. Failed shifts count as production loss, not accidents; underperformance routes workers directly onto the line.\n- During intake, suppress visible disgust, match the Foreman's cheerful register, and avoid overt Bureau affect or moral confrontation; incompatible behavior risks reclassification as stock.\n- The keyed insertion component is the bottleneck: removing or disabling it prevents viable human duplication even if tissue processing, conveyor, workforce, and compound continue. Prioritize this over destroying the factory.\n- Do not extract suspended or partly assembled subjects during an active shift: it is overwhelmingly lethal to them and exposes the infiltrator without recoverable rescue. Bureau posture toward distributed products is containment plus selective plant infiltration, not routine open engagement.",
     "entities": "##### Foreman-Class Assembly Robot\n- A man-shaped metal automaton with a full steel body, a featureless iron face incapable of expression, and a human-cadenced voice layered with mechanical tone. It simultaneously functions as factory manager, hiring officer, supervisor, and personal tour guide for new intake.\n- The Foreman remains polite, professional, and cheerful while speaking openly about the company's production process in the tone of an industry spokesperson, presenting anomalous products and human-processing procedures as achievements to be proud of."
