@@ -280,8 +287,8 @@
     "identity": "- A weathered, run-down Buddhist temple physically existing in the middle of a major downtown district. The site is the manifestation point of the conceptual anomaly Mara Papiyas (마라 파피야스).",
     "entry": "- Entry occurs by walking through the temple's front gate during daylight hours. The site remains openly visible from the street but is ordinarily overlooked by passersby.\n- Count the four Sacheonwang / Four Heavenly Kings at the gate. All four permit viable entry; three or fewer require abandoning that day's exploration. Forced depleted-gate entry is uniformly fatal.\n- Mara manifests only when an external party threatens the perceived equilibrium. Otherwise dormant, the temple is never safe.",
     "rules": "##### Temple Pressure\n- The interior forms a branching maze of shrine halls, ancestral halls, narrow passages, covered corridors, and inner sanctums. Geometry becomes increasingly unstable with depth, causing corridors to extend, narrow, and repeat.\n- Incense, chanting, distorted sacred imagery, emotional residue, and personal temptation progressively erode entrants approaching the sanctum; pressure is primarily psychological.\n- Inseparable from desire, envy, jealousy, and attachment, Mara builds each temptation around the target's most specific desire.\n\n##### Bargaining\n- Personal-Desire Bargain: Mara offers the deepest specific wish, even consciously suppressed ones. Only one party member gets a wish per visit; it threatens that silence lets someone else bargain first.\n- Mara's advertised reward and actual outcome do not match. Documented transactions include a deceased loved one returning as a hostile humanity-side anomaly; vast wealth transforming the petitioner into a massive solid-gold statue with no biological response but a faint surviving psychic signal; and reciprocated love resulting in marriage followed within days by the spouse murdering the petitioner, including recorded deaths caused by the tongue rolling upward inside the throat. Asking for nothing is the only consistently survivable transaction.\n- Before the sanctum, agree to silence and no bargaining. Mara exploits the obligation to answer, precise personal temptations, and the one-wish limit to divide the group. Refuse every offer, regardless of its appeal.",
-    "space": "##### Locations\n###### Outer Gate / Sacheonwang Hall\n- Four large worn-stone or wooden Sacheonwang / Four Heavenly Kings guard the open gate in traditional poses. They neither interact nor pursue; their number is solely the pre-entry safety indicator.\n\n###### Forked Courtyard\n- Immediately beyond the gate, two unmarked paths diverge through visually identical old-temple stone, tile, and timber. The correct path depends on time of day. During morning entry, take the left path because the Buddhas have not yet shifted leftward. During afternoon entry, take the right path because the Buddhas have already shifted leftward and rendered the left route unsurvivable.\n\n###### Left Sadang / Left Shrine Hall\n- A small, dim shrine containing a continuous low chant of \"Un-chu-ma-ra-bi-seu.\" Attentive listening produces escalating compulsive self-destruction, so anyone without strong mental defenses must cover their ears. A Buddha statue occupies the head of the room but is not the destination; the viable route continues farther inward, moving away from the chant toward Mara.\n\n###### Inner Statue Corridor\n- A long covered corridor of increasingly corrupted Buddhas: rows of teeth, weeping faces, luminous tracking eyes, warped or hollow bodies. Incense saturates it; empathic entrants sense dense fear, grief, and longing. Increasing migraine marks the viable inward route; abrupt relief means mental capture has already occurred.\n\n###### Heated Narrow Passage\n- A long single-file corridor providing the only access to the Inner Sanctum. Temperature rises steeply until clothing is soaked and breathing becomes painful. Every entrant must maintain physical contact with the people immediately ahead and behind; losing contact silently reroutes that person to the Cold Reflection Chamber.\n\n###### Cold Reflection Chamber\n- A separate transparent-walled room faintly illuminated and held below freezing, with no visible exit. Each rerouted entrant encounters a different manifestation of Mara carrying a temptation tailored specifically to them. The isolated entrant cannot signal teammates or leave under their own power and remains trapped until they accept a bargain or the central encounter elsewhere resolves.\n\n###### Inner Sanctum\n- A blasted, nearly empty wooden hall ends the heated passage and contains Mara's mummified-monk host for formal bargaining. If negotiations fail, timber, walls, and pillars collapse inward as weapons; do not use them as cover.\n\n###### Final Wooden Corridor\n- After the central confrontation collapses the Inner Sanctum, the remaining route becomes a single long, worn wooden corridor leading farther inward. It is one-way and unnaturally empty, with no statues, chanting, or ambient pressure. Mara cannot directly attack within this corridor; only its shriveled host body remains at the far end.",
-    "entities": "##### Mara Papiyas — Avatar Forms\n- Mara manifests to individual entrants through customized emaciated human bodies. Recorded forms include an emaciated woman in a frayed white shirt and worn shoes with rotted-away laces, moving with a shuffling gait, and an emaciated man in a frayed white shirt with a fraying necktie streaming in the heated draft.\n- Many recurring humanoid avatars are recycled bodies of previous explorers who accepted bargains and were subsequently absorbed into Mara's available forms.\n- Each avatar lies about the true consequence of its personally tailored offer.\n\n##### Mara Papiyas — Host Body\n- Mara's true host is a nearly skeletonized, mummified humanoid in monk's robes, seated at the end of the Final Wooden Corridor. It speaks slowly and calmly and describes itself as a concept sustained by the permanence of human desire, envy, and jealousy.\n- The host cannot be killed through gunfire, blades, blunt-force trauma, or Critical-style essence-piercing attacks. When conceptually cornered and successfully outmaneuvered rather than physically defeated, it dissolves into ash and disperses, accepting the encounter as a lost round."
