, a side lever starts it, and full destructive operation takes time. The notebook's nightmare-awakening theory is unverified; do not turn its despair into a confirmed return procedure.\n\n###### Docks, Yard, and Kim Seong-jin\n- Front Gate / Outbound Delivery Dock: trucks reverse in; workers handcart canned-meat boxes into their beds. Hiding aboard is physically possible but carries the victim farther into the monster world, not automatically home.\n- Rear Gate / Inbound Supply Dock: trucks deliver humans. A lone driver commonly leaves the cab to open and unload the bed, creating the documented opportunity to steal an inbound vehicle.\n- The flat yard mixes dirt with flesh-like villi. Debris and refuse offer limited cover; the open plain beyond favors fast Butcher pursuers. A rear outlet continuously discharges greywater with no visible contamination, drinkable when no safer source is available.\n- Kim Seong-jin was a long-term civilian survivor, not an entity, and has since escaped. He hid in a hand-dug spider hole with a salvaged monster light, eating outside villi and drinking wastewater. Isolation caused screaming fits, finger-chewing, and abrupt mood reversals, yet he learned Butcher behavior, machine and bell timing, truck schedules, outbound product traffic, and the rear supply lane.",
     "survival": "##### Wider World, Return Leads, and Core\n- The rear road crosses a plain toward the Black Curtain, a vertical sheet of total darkness through which vehicles disappear. It is a dimensional boundary, but whether it leads to the human world, elsewhere in monster territory, or another otherworld is unknown. A stolen inbound truck offers mobility toward it, not a guaranteed return.\n- The Intestine Sky is a separate sky-scale organism, not the Factory Core. Its ecological function is unknown. Sufficiently strong sealing or suturing-type effects can affect its organic tissue; this does not establish the same vulnerability for the Core. Removing the sky reveals a distant Black Tower; no associated Black Dogs occur in the observed factory-side environment.\n- Another unconfirmed lead relates removing one's own corpse from the anomalous space to return. Method, destination, and conditions are unknown. Neither this nor grinder death is a usable verified escape procedure.\n- No ordinary victim has a verified independent return route. Outside contact or intervention, unresolved dimensional routes, or factory destruction may be needed; physical departure from the plant only ends immediate enclosure.\n- The Factory Core, a wrinkled red sphere somewhere inside, is the plant's life. Damage regenerates in about three seconds, sustaining it despite destroyed workers, machinery, or sections.\n- Confirmed full clear: breach the Core with sufficient force and implant Cheongak Mary Hospital prescription medicine in exposed inner tissue before that roughly three-second window closes. The foreign anomalous substance kills it from within and the facility fails. Raw high-end force without Core neutralization is insufficient.\n- If a successful-clear attempt permits, recover Disposal Room belongings for identification and record verified discoveries in the notebook in case the operation fails and another victim arrives."
