+   "keys": "원숭이 꿈 괴담, 원숭이 꿈, 몽키가든, Monkey Dream",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Abduction and Railway Cycle\n- A subway abduction anomaly wearing the Japanese internet tale of the Monkey Dream: a narrator repeatedly dreams of riding with dazed passengers, a broadcast announces the station occupants' deaths, monkeys massacre them, and the final recurrence warns, \"Next time, you will not escape.\" Here abduction is physical, not dreaming.\n- A vampire colony has seized the anomaly. Its monkeys and Conductor now use the massacre structure to hunt humans and supply blood.\n- Anomaly-detection GPS marks an active point in an otherwise normal metropolitan station as a RED DOT. Approaching it causes implausibly thinning crowds, cold air, and vanished ambient sound; crossing instantly transfers victims to the dark platform. Commuters may enter accidentally: \"I was about to take the subway when the scenery suddenly changed.\" Withdrawal before reaching the point can avoid abduction.\n- Train arrival, the Conductor's massacre announcement, killing, and departure repeat on a railway schedule. Intervals between trains are safest for moving or communicating. Functioning station payphones connect outside only then; outgoing calls display `[□□□□□□□]`, a live distress clue. Report the station name.",
     "space": "##### Railway and Hunting Force\n###### Dark Platform and Internal Stations\n- Unlit, nearly silent platforms are covered with broad patches of dried black blood. Multiple internal stations absent from ordinary metropolitan maps imitate restrooms, information booths, shops, and stairs, all deserted. No staircase reaches the surface; there is no normal station exit to reality.\n- Do not voluntarily board. Those already aboard can get off at the next stop and hide away from doors and expected monkey movement, then act during the interval.\n- Dazed Passengers are ordinary victims sitting or standing blankly with little resistance even during slaughter. This condition is neither instant nor universal: newly taken people may still run, hide, leave at stops, call outside, and time their actions.\n\n###### Train / Carving Station (도려내기 역)\n- Arrival uses the ordinary announcement, \"The train is now arriving.\" Cars resemble an abattoir, strewn with blood, organs, minced remains, dismembered bodies, and partial corpses. Some monkeys remain between stops, mutilating or playing with bodies.\n- The train is an anomalous imitation, requiring neither realistic driving nor normal infrastructure. Inter-car doors can be forced, but after departure the railway behaves as a closed rotating circuit; ordinary travel cannot return home.\n- \"Next station, Carving. Carving Station.\" Internal station broadcasts correspond to the monkeys' work in the massacre cycle.\n\n###### Vampire Monkeys\n- At least twelve armed monkeys, with grotesquely bulging forward-facing eyes, vertical feline pupils, and about a hundred curved blade-like fangs. They carry knives and other cutting implements, grin, laugh `\"Kihihihi\"`, play with severed heads, and deliberately mince living victims. Dismemberment, mutilation, and draining serve both recreation and colony supply.\n- Their fusion with the tale may disrupt ordinary vampire-detection effects without removing vampire weaknesses: garlic dissolves flesh like strong acid, holy power burns, and crosses, silver, and equivalent counters work. Once this protection is overcome, they can be killed like ordinary armed animals. Heavily outmatched survivors may panic, discard weapons, trample one another, and flee through the cars.\n- Direct combat without appropriate vampire counters is unfavorable.\n\n###### Conductor and Route Authority\n- A Vampire Monkey in full railway uniform, normally the only one able to speak human language. It schedules the train, oversees killing, and delivers harvested blood to the hidden colony terminal. Its polite service announcement is: \"We will now begin carving out the customers in the station.\"\n- Killing it does not give a replacement driver access to its complete route; they remain on the circulating internal line. Its hat carries the vacant role's authority. Wearing it after its death transfers the Conductor role, restores full-route access, and makes the colony terminal a valid destination.\n\n##### Colony and Blood Supply\n- The terminal route emerges from enclosed subway space into a vast dark expanse. Beyond rocky mountains, dense pointed buildings form a compact vampire city with specialized facilities, organized logistics, armed personnel, and central leadership, not a makeshift refuge.\n- Normally such a large population would betray itself through local disappearances and overhunting. Distant railway abductions conceal the settlement while feeding it: massacre and collection → large tanks in the train's rear cars → Conductor transport → dedicated uniformed reception, unloading, and security → Central Hall storage.\n- Colony Ghouls are vampire-controlled servitors patrolling portions of the railway and settlement approaches, intercepting intruders beyond the Monkey Dream's own killing zones.\n- Separate Colony Forces act as guards, cargo crews, patrols, and coordinated armed response. Automatic rifles and other firearms supplement vampire physiques; some individuals manifest bat-like wings. Blood and secrecy limit force size, but it is sufficient to defend the city, routes, and shipments.\n\n###### Human Livestock Pens\n- Restrained captives are repeatedly drained, with numerous extraction wounds. They are deliberately nourished to preserve body mass and long-term blood production rather than killed immediately.\n- Prolonged captivity devastates them psychologically. Some cannot speak coherently, stand unaided, respond normally to humans, or recognize rescue.\n\n###### Central Hall / Kenoorn (케노른)\n- The central major facility receives blood and concentrates organization and defense. Under major attack, surviving vampires gather or retreat there.\n- Kenoorn rules the city and is its highest confirmed authority, far stronger and more experienced than ordinary residents. Partial monstrous transformation grants powerful claws; blood-based explosive attacks violently repel opponents. He understands anti-vampire weapons and can immediately excise silver-contaminated flesh before damage spreads.",
