    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Board Game and Guest Status\n- A physical board game contains a fantasy-park otherworld: gaudy, old-fashioned attractions, mascots, parades, prize shops, brass-band music, and exaggerated family imagery. Enjoyment is enforced even through mutilation, death, and abusive mascot demands. Parties ignorant of the User Guide seldom finish without death, disappearance, or integration.\n- The box, \"Yukoae Theme Park! ~A Joyful Fantasy-Land Trip~\", holds a capsule of colored pieces matching the required participant count. Each person draws one; color assigns team and starting territory. Withdrawal is unreliable once drawn. When the last required piece is taken and the board unfolded, everyone enters simultaneously.\n- Entrants awaken in assigned zones with paper Fantasyland Admission Wristbands bearing three empty stamp slots. This is recognition as a legitimate guest, not decoration.\n- To clear, every teammate must physically board three qualifying major attractions together, preserve the three stamped slots, and use the north exit. Carrying an unconscious teammate aboard counts. Fastest qualifying teams may receive a mascot-selected gift-shop prize, ranging from ordinary branded souvenirs to anomalous items.",
     "rules": "##### User Guide and Enforcement\nThe Guide has ten numbered articles; only the following seven are mechanically established.\n\n1. Keep the Admission Wristband clean and intact. Loss, damage, destruction, or forced removal immediately revokes guest status: the person becomes an intruder, thief, criminal, or potential staff member.\n2. Same-color teammates must stay together, within approximately five meters outside active attraction boarding/riding. Near the limit a thin red leash-like cord appears and tightens; exceeding it strangles. Closing ranks removes it.\n3. Crying, wailing, screaming, and intense negative displays do not suit the park and are forbidden.\n4. Theme and ruling mascot define each zone; the mascot's absolute territorial authority overrides ordinary park logic.\n5. Changed mascot design and environmental color mean a new territory. The previous mascot cannot exist there or follow across its boundary.\n6. Countless observing eyes remember guest behavior.\n7. Cheer parades joyfully. Everything in them must be enjoyed without visible negative judgment.\n\n- Music, rides, performances, and parades continue through casualties. Cursing, visible disgust, recoiling, and other serious negative reactions can instead freeze nearby machinery and silence music. After a brief counted pause, every guest, worker, mascot, and parade figure turns to the offender. Quickly ending the display can restore the performance; continuing brings punishment.\n- Maintain controlled behavior, smile and clap lightly at parades, avoid prolonged mascot eye contact, and neither touch nor collect grotesque debris. Keep incapacitated teammates with the group rather than abandoning them.\n- Cheerful attraction notices can state literal hazards. Real ride mechanisms exist—emergency buttons, panels, powered gates, service equipment—but a ride may suppress ordinary emergency stopping. Technical work is possible when mascot observation is avoided, not automatically safe.\n\n##### Facilities, Staff, and Prize\n- One silent, empty-eyed humanoid Attraction-Operator Mascot per ride stamps wristbands during boarding. Operators normally avoid direct attack but can report unusual conduct to the ruler.\n- Zone-uniformed Information-Booth Mascots gesture routine directions to recognized guests. They are comparatively non-hostile until pressed for inappropriate, restricted, or member-only requests.\n- Locker rooms, restroom backs, and service corridors have less routine mascot traffic and can support regrouping, treatment, or ritual preparation. Border gaps and backstage routes expose hollow decorative walls, dormant gates, and equipment; ordinary emergency panels may restore powered-down mechanisms.\n- Gift shops award fast-clear prizes. Public-use phones and snack trucks provide access to mundane supplies such as food, water, torches, salt, and marshmallows.\n- Good Friend: a soft plush prize activated with flame, about 100 ml water, one spoon of salt, one clean coin, and an object meaningfully tied to a friend. Completion permanently anchors an other-side mind in the doll. Materials from other anomalies can substitute but distort which \"friend\" responds.\n- For standard departure, all teammates must still be recognized guests with three qualifying stamps each. Preserve wristbands and team proximity, then proceed to the north gate; neither a territory change nor Membership fulfills that condition.",
