    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Exposure and Dream Scenario\n- The horror game \"In the Black Shadow\" overwrites a school-shaped dream modeled on Segwang Technical High School, which cannot reliably be found in reality. It reconstructs graduation eve after students desecrated a rear-garden buried talisman and summoned Teacher; the fifth-floor ceremony became mass sacrifice.\n- The vector is \"In the Black Shadow.txt\", sometimes inside pirated collections of supposed 2000s horror novels. Despite novel-sized apparent length, it opens to one sentence saying everything happened on graduation day, then corrupted glyphs, an unreadable-file error, and self-deletion.\n- Reading exposes the reader; later sleep may bring entry, though eligibility varies and identical exposure does not consistently admit everyone. Entrants wake separately in random rooms wearing their own real alma mater's uniform, not Segwang's.\n- Deliberately placing objects under the pillow brings them into the dream, allowing preparation. A reliable hands-free headlamp is particularly useful because it cannot easily be dropped; preferably carry at least two independent light sources.\n- Foreign entrants are errors in an already-running game, not legitimate original players. Native students, rooms, faculty, and graduation schedule continue their scenario. Credentialed death provides one ordinary exit; a distinct True Ending resolves the ceremony through a valid student role.",
     "rules": "##### Light, Gaze, and Recognition\n- Perpetual night and broken/flickering ceiling lights alternate visibility with total shadow. Direct observation by any living observer blocks a student's gross locomotion, not fine motion such as handles, posture, or head turns. Even an immobile injured witness can pin one.\n- Once every relevant sightline breaks—blink, darkness, obstruction, or flash blindness—students move fast enough to cross a room and kill within a fraction of a second. Keep one eye open by alternating blinks; pairs can move back-to-back along a wall watching front and rear. Softly coordinate sightline changes and never shine into a teammate's eyes.\n- Student action against a victim can establish persistent targeting, called recognition. A conscious student watching another's nameplate being harvested likewise becomes a persistent pursuer. Blood or fresh-use traces inside curled fingers can betray a recent attack beneath stillness.\n- Noise carries across rooms and doors: shouting, screams, loud speech, and profanity attract attention. Move quietly rather than blindly running. Successful floor changes usually stop ordinary pursuit by students from the previous floor, providing partial separation.\n- Ordinary blunt or edged force can injure and disable students, leaving severe casualties immobile even unwatched. Mass improvised attacks are poor strategy without a specific objective: noise, recognition, blackouts, and crowding do not solve the school.\n- Student deaths can trigger a calm PA announcement, several seconds of mandatory school-wide darkness, low funeral music, and convergence toward the disturbance. In a full blackout, lower the head and remain still and controlled; visual locking is unavailable and frantic fighting worsens risk.",
