     "identity": "##### Sealed City and Day of Disaster\n- An entire Korean special city classified as an extinction-class supernatural disaster. The Bureau's strongest cognition-sealing curse erased it from human memory: ordinary people cannot perceive, remember, rediscover, or intentionally navigate to it. The city remains physically present behind the seal.\n- On the Day of Disaster, a profane intrusion spread like an epidemic while the city's supernatural protection failed at its root. Crowds chanted of paradise and heaven, then fused into swollen, mucous-skinned multi-person masses. Tens of thousands fled underground.\n- Contamination, collective terror, desperate wishes, and the affected places' original concepts transformed the infrastructure. Stations became independent anomalies shaped by what they had been and what people demanded of them.\n- The local Bureau branch was destroyed during rescue and triage; the national response sealed the city. The disaster never truly ended: the surface remains catastrophic, station variances continue, and something associated with the outbreak still grows toward the city center.\n- Segwang is a persistent disaster environment, not one anomaly with a universal clear. Terminating a station neither ends the city nor automatically changes the others. Keep expeditions focused on a particular rescue, intelligence target, or station objective; distinguish safe passage from destruction of a governing mechanism for termination.",
     "entry": "##### Entry, Death, and Claims\n- Entry requires an anomalous route bypassing the cognition seal. Every route first delivers its entrant to Segwang Station's Platform. From that initial foothold, follow Segwang Station's boarding procedure to reach the operating subway and other stations.\n- A geomantic-node dream-channel well can activate transfer while an entrant is inside or directly touching it. The dream-self arrives on that Platform while the real body remains asleep outside until the stay ends.\n- Transit systems or passages in unrelated anomalies can connect through Adjacent Tale routes, sometimes accidentally. Non-well entrants likewise arrive on Segwang Station's Platform, human-shaped and physically restored.\n- Death generally ejects a victim beyond the seal, allowing some repeat explorers to re-equip and return. It is not universally safe: fatal dream-self injuries appear identically on the sleeping real body even if death ends the stay.\n- A station can instead retain someone who dies through its completed process, incorporating them into the anomaly. The Scale Tribunal's condemned are one example. Access-route consequences and station claims must be distinguished from ordinary ejection.",
-    "space": "##### Subway, Surface, and Station Network\n- Roads, homes, shops, and public facilities survive physically above ground, but sustained habitation is catastrophically unsafe. Limit surface movement to objectives unreachable by subway.\n- The seven-station circle line serves major industrial and residential districts. Only its inner loop operates; the outer loop is dead. Automatic trains are the sole reliable inter-station transport and the principal human foothold.\n- During a ride, passengers appear in the physical state they had on first entering the station system. Later wounds, missing limbs, and bodily changes are visually suppressed only: there is no actual healing, and the true condition returns immediately on disembarkation.\n- The seven stops comprise Segwang Station and six stations with time-of-day names; the latter replace pre-disaster names. Each station and its associated facilities has independent rules, clear conditions, and possible termination methods:\n  1. Segwang Station / Forest of the Dying Path (세광역 / 임종의 숲길): roughly seven thousand evacuees collectively chose death and became a forest of hanged trees.\n  2. Midnight Station / Body Casino (자정역 / 신체 카지노): gambling with coins exchanged for possessions and human anatomy.\n  3. Deep Night Station / Hanbit Library (한밤역 / 한빛도서관): a refurbished station preserving books, past people, places, and the demolished Segwang Technical High School.\n  4. Dusk Station / Conscience Sales Stand (황혼역 / 양심판매대): an unmanned flea market made into a burning hell by years of unpaid theft and conscience debt.\n  5. Afternoon Station / Blood Broadcasting Station (오후역 / 혈액 방송국): Delusion Home Shopping occupies studios rented by Blood Broadcasting Station for sapient blood.\n  6. Midday Station / Nap Shelter (한낮역 / 낮잠용 쉼터): a permanent-noon residential welcome that puts sleepers to permanent rest.\n  7. Morning Station / Scale Tribunal (아침역 / 저울 재판소): beneath the Segwang Provincial Court, the former underground Bureau branch has become a tribunal.\n- Each station has its own Yukwae Research Institute facility below it: Segwang houses the Core Layer, and the other six have subordinate branches. Institute access requires termination of the station's anomaly to reach the opposite platform, then a valid Segwang Transit Corporation Employee ID at the machine-room/service-door panel. Each door leads to that station's own facility; existing local access barriers still apply.\n- Before entering a station anomaly, identify both its original place-concept and the symbolic authority of its current name. Survival may suffice for passage; termination is a separate objective.",
+    "space": "##### Subway, Surface, and Station Network\n- Roads, homes, shops, and public facilities survive physically above ground, but sustained habitation is catastrophically unsafe. Limit surface movement to objectives unreachable by subway.\n- The seven-station circle line serves major industrial and residential districts. Only its inner loop operates; the outer loop is dead. Automatic trains are the sole reliable inter-station transport and the principal human foothold.\n- During a ride, passengers appear in the physical state they had on first entering the station system. Later wounds, missing limbs, and bodily changes are visually suppressed only: there is no actual healing, and the true condition returns immediately on disembarkation.\n- The seven stops comprise Segwang Station and six stations with time-of-day names; the latter replace pre-disaster names. Each station and its associated facilities has independent rules, clear conditions, and possible termination methods:\n  1. Segwang Station / Forest of the Dying Path (세광역 / 임종의 숲길): roughly seven thousand evacuees collectively chose death and became a forest of hanged trees.\n  2. Midnight Station / Body Casino (자정역 / 신체 카지노): gambling with coins exchanged for possessions and human anatomy.\n  3. Deep Night Station / Hanbit Library (한밤역 / 한빛도서관): a refurbished station preserving books, past people, places, and the demolished Segwang Technical High School.\n  4. Dusk Station / Conscience Stall (황혼역 / 양심판매대): an unmanned flea market made into a burning hell by years of unpaid theft and conscience debt.\n  5. Afternoon Station / Blood Broadcasting Station (오후역 / 혈액 방송국): Delusion Home Shopping occupies studios rented by Blood Broadcasting Station for sapient blood.\n  6. Midday Station / Nap Shelter (한낮역 / 낮잠용 쉼터): a permanent-noon residential welcome that puts sleepers to permanent rest.\n  7. Morning Station / Scale Tribunal (아침역 / 저울 재판소): beneath the Segwang Provincial Court, the former underground Bureau branch has become a tribunal.\n- Each station has its own Yukwae Research Institute facility below it: Segwang houses the Core Layer, and the other six have subordinate branches. Institute access requires termination of the station's anomaly to reach the opposite platform, then a valid Segwang Transit Corporation Employee ID at the machine-room/service-door panel. Each door leads to that station's own facility; existing local access barriers still apply.\n- Before entering a station anomaly, identify both its original place-concept and the symbolic authority of its current name. Survival may suffice for passage; termination is a separate objective.",
     "entities": "##### Shelter Train Community\n- Day-of-Disaster survivors inhabit the continuously circulating inner-loop train; the principal shelter occupies two connected cars with about twenty-five residents. Perpetual transit and restored outward appearance offer their least unsafe long-term refuge.\n- Unknown boarders may meet mop-handle, tape, and scavenged-material pikes and orders to return to the platform. Once admitted, a clean newcomer attracts intense crowding and questions about the outside, entry, and routes through the seal.\n- Without useful escape information, excitement quickly becomes demands to disclose food and equipment, an unofficial lodging toll, disarming, or extortion of anyone too passive, polite, or weak to resist. These are human commuters made defensive by years of scarcity, not inherently predatory entities.\n- Front and Rear Cars depend on the same shelter but disagree over leadership and supplies. Expect exclusion, interrogation, material demands, and factional friction before cooperation. A recurring, unverified rumor of a new seal breach sustains hope after years on the closed line.\n\n###### The Conductor — Front Car\n- A man around his fifties, in worn transit workwear and scavenged shelter layers. Small restless eyes, habitual forehead sweat, stress-flushed blotchy face, and unstable jaw movements when cornered mark him.\n- Maintains control by intimidation, hoarding, and threats to abandon riders at hostile stops. He values his authority over supplies and survival decisions despite others' cost, repeatedly framing exclusion as operational necessity and clashing with the Rear Car.\n\n###### Station Clerk / Station Attendant — Rear Car\n- A woman around her forties, with tired but alert eyes, restrained expression, and a habit of listening before replying. Functional station-duty clothes are layered for cold, prolonged platform work.\n- Leads through mutual aid, shared resources, and collective decisions; manages scarcity, lodging, vending permissions, and vulnerable riders' protection. Negotiation is firm, concise, and rarely openly emotional.\n\n##### Surface Mass and Bureau Remnants\n- Citizen Cocoon Mass: citizens fused by the original contagion form a major surface biohazard. Individual bodies remain visible on the outer shell; deeper swollen tissue erases personal and anatomical boundaries. It grabs nearby intruders indiscriminately, absorbing them as cocoon material rather than distinct infected people.\n- Bureau Survivors: remnants of the response force trapped when the national seal replaced completed rescue. Their branch suffered catastrophic losses triaging the subway exodus. Some retain pre-seal knowledge unknown to train residents; its final surviving knowledge is entombed around Morning Station and the Scale Tribunal. Those who regard the seal as abandonment may be institutionally hostile to present-day Bureau agents."
    },
