@@ -615,12 +622,12 @@
    "keys": "Segwang Station, Forest of the Dying, 세광역, 임종의 숲, 임종의 숲길",
    "fields": {
     "identity": "##### Mandatory Arrival and Founding\n- A station sub-anomaly within sealed Segwang Special City. Every successful entry, regardless of route or method, ends here: entrants materialize unconscious, sprawled on the Platform, then awaken without experiencing the transfer. They never initially awaken in the Concourse, another station, or the surface.\n- The plaque bears the paid-advertisement-style subtitle \"Forest of the Dying Path.\" Its identity merged with the real-world suicide hotspot \"■■■ Forest,\" crossed by the line.\n- Nearest major stop to City Hall, the wider disaster's origin, it received roughly seven thousand evacuees and became the line's largest stronghold. Failed communications, exhausted food, continuing surface catastrophe, and absent rescue drove them to collective suicide. The station varied around their choice; the Forest is that population, not a separate predator that killed it.\n- Some hanging bodies bear pen-written palm testaments. One reads:\n\n  No one is coming to save us  \n  Seven thousand were abandoned  \n  We want to run  \n  but there is no way out  \n  so we become trees instead\n\n- The Forest recruits later entrants into the same conclusion through despair, suggestion, separation, and surrender. City Hall's proximity also makes the station important for reaching the unresolved disaster's center.",
-    "space": "##### Platform and Forest Concourse\n- The subway shelters entrants from the surface's extinction-class disaster, which does not normally project directly underground; the station's own anomaly remains active.\n- The Platform has ordinary subway architecture and dim but usable light. It is the main staging, rest, regrouping, and fallback area while the Forest stays upstairs. The opposite-track side remains collapsed and unreachable while the Forest is active; a staircase at the usable Platform's end ascends to the Concourse.\n- Above are earth, dead leaves, trees, and dense humid fog. Thick trunks alternate with hanging human bodies whose clothing carries years of dust; corpses are too numerous to count. A blindly reached-for branch may be a human foot. Sound is unnaturally dead apart from transit audio and recruitment voices.\n- The etiquette board stands near the entrance stairs; the cash transit-card machine and turnstiles lie deeper inside, requiring passage through the Forest. Protective charms and similar wards rapidly mold and physically collapse while carried.\n\n##### Station Office and Institute Access\n- A reinforced-glass door separates the ordinary concourse Station Office from public space. Desks, cabinets, lost property, and transit administrative materials remain; a Segwang Transit Corporation Employee ID can be obtained from personnel, remains, or stored property.\n- Terminating the Forest makes the opposite-direction platform accessible. There, a staff-only machine/communications-room steel door accepts that ID and opens into the Institute Core Layer beneath Segwang Station. An ID alone does not make the platform reachable. Ordinary train departure follows the registration procedure above and does not require terminating the Forest.",
+    "space": "##### Platform and Forest Concourse\n- The subway shelters entrants from the surface's extinction-class disaster, which does not normally project directly underground; the station's own anomaly remains active.\n- The Platform has ordinary subway architecture and dim but usable light. It is the main staging, rest, regrouping, and fallback area while the Forest stays upstairs. The opposite-track side remains collapsed and unreachable while the Forest is active; a staircase at the usable Platform's end ascends to the Concourse.\n- Above are earth, dead leaves, trees, and dense humid fog. Thick trunks alternate with hanging human bodies whose clothing carries years of dust; corpses are too numerous to count. A blindly reached-for branch may be a human foot. Sound is unnaturally dead apart from transit audio and recruitment voices.\n- The etiquette board stands near the entrance stairs; the cash transit-card machine and turnstiles lie deeper inside, requiring passage through the Forest. Protective charms and similar wards rapidly mold and physically collapse while carried.\n\n##### Station Office and Institute Access\n- A reinforced-glass door separates the ordinary concourse Station Office from public space. Desks, cabinets, lost property, and transit administrative materials remain; a Segwang Transit Corporation Employee ID can be obtained from personnel, remains, or stored property.\n- Terminating the Forest makes the opposite-direction platform accessible. There, a staff-only machine/communications-room steel door accepts that ID and opens into the Institute Core Layer beneath Segwang Station. An ID alone does not make the platform reachable. Ordinary train departure follows the registration procedure below and does not require terminating the Forest.",
     "rules": "##### Etiquette: Two Speakers\nThe complete board reads:\n\n1. Do not break the branches\n2. Stand too close to the screen doors and you will see something strange.\n3. Run near the turnstiles and an exit appears.\n4. Do not become separated from your party\n5. Do not hang yourself from the trees\n6. The disorderly within the station are in the fog.\n7. Trains bound for ■■ no longer stop here.\n\n- Punctuation identifies the speaker. Period-ending Rules 2, 3, 6, and 7 come from the functioning Station infrastructure: informational and literally true, without promising safety. Unpunctuated Rules 1, 4, and 5 are Forest imperatives, revealing what it seeks to impose or prevent.\n- Rule 5 addresses people without prior suicidal intent because the Forest means to manufacture that intent. Reject its framing and do not use its nooses.\n- Directly read notice-board information loses retention once the reader looks away, fading \"like fog seeping in.\" A whole party can forget Rule 3 before reaching the turnstiles; even awareness of forgetting can fade during the realization. Comprehension remains possible. Immediately copy, continuously recite, or otherwise externalize vital information away from the board's channel.\n\n##### Recruitment, Fog, and Escalation\n- Inhaling Concourse mist introduces whispers or news-like audio into the ambience. It reports future deaths as completed events: unidentified people matching the party's number, location, and circumstances supposedly abandoned train boarding and hanged themselves near the passage. It eventually asks directly, \"Don't you want to give up too?\"\n- Empty nooses wait among the trees, effectively one per exposed entrant. Further loops appear around each person's eye level as the voice intensifies and surrender feels increasingly appropriate. Prior suicidal intent is unnecessary.\n- Fog thickens with time, disturbance, and exposure. Physically close companions can become unable to see or touch one another despite negligible distance; apparent teammate silhouettes may be false, and reaching for a shoulder may contact a hanging corpse. Keep together, control noise, and distrust unconfirmed shapes.\n- Rule 6 links disorder directly to the fog. A sufficiently roused station lets it pour down into the Platform, ending that area's relative safety. Passenger registration also starts this extraction escalation. Once fog breaches the Platform, overhead nooses can catch necks and violently pull victims upward.",
     "survival": "##### Rule 3's Real, Dangerous Exit\n- Running near the turnstiles manifests a narrow upward \"Exit\" staircase (■번 출구). It reaches a genuine surface-level shutter barricaded from inside with stacked debris and marked by dried bloody refugee footprints from the Day of Disaster.\n- The Station fulfills its statement while omitting that the destination is the extinction-class surface. Looking toward the manifested Exit exposes the viewer to something dangerous associated with the route or beyond it. Do not trigger it; if it appears, avert attention, reverse direction immediately, and regain the Platform. It is not the ordinary survival route.\n\n##### Train Registration and Departure\n- Physical presence on the Platform does not establish passenger status. If nobody has tapped through the turnstiles, trains announce that the stop is skipped for absence of passengers and pass without stopping.\n1. Briefly enter the Concourse and find the card machine.\n2. Pay cash for one single-use transit card per intended passenger.\n3. Tap every party member through the entry-direction turnstiles.\n4. Return directly to the Platform after the final registration.\n5. Board the next stopping train before its doors close and the advancing fog compromises boarding.\n- Each tap registers its holder and begins the Forest's extraction escalation. Avoid unnecessary Concourse time or delay after registration; if fog arrives first, prioritize immediate boarding against overhead noose attacks."
    },
