     "title": "Namhae Branch Appendix: Facilities and Registered Uh-doom",
     "body": "#### Facilities\n- Worker Zone: assembly hall split into X/Y/Z pens like a cattle shed, dorms, canteen, store (5,000 won a cigarette), vending-machine clinic at extreme prices; wiretaps and CCTV with occasional blind spots.\n- Leisure Zone (Sundays): a tacky bulb-lit rural night street of mostly unstaffed shops at several times outside prices: Namhae Bar, Happy Lottery, Rhythm Karaoke, Sleep Care (massage chairs, Baekilmong hair-loss pills, unprescribed drugs, \"Painkiller – 300,000 (EXTRA STRONG!)\"), arcade, comic room, and a Religious Activity corridor (one faith per room, Sunday fortune-teller, last room a dried rite table with a pig's head). \"Staff Only\" doors hide staff areas. Nobody steals; everyone has seen the price.\n- Containment Zone: by mine cart; identical dark grey doors, red-lit cells, some earth-floored.\n- Staff Zone: 2000s public-corporation offices, sectors such as B-5 and B-9, storerooms, a Worker management room behind a one-way mirror.\n- Old Facility: sealed behind earth walls and a disused staff bathhouse since a cost-cutting renovation six years ago (which split staff and containment areas with one door, below HQ standards). Steel corridors, hand-wheel doors, surveillance gallery, emergency exits, doors with a distinctive \"Staff Only\" handle crest, and a central control system bootable in safe mode. A former manager's office, administrator account, and early Uh-doom documents remain.\n- Loudspeaker: \"Good morning! All Workers, please prepare for today's work~\", \"Roll call in ten minutes. Get rich today too~\", \"Lunch time! Eat well and make lots of money this afternoon~\", \"When you're desperate: Dream Money, Dream Life!\", \"Leisure Zone opening. Fighting this week too! Get rich!\" Emergency alarm: \"[EMERGENCY!] All employees still inside, evacuate via the escape routes!\" Workers are told the old mine misfires and to ignore it; it is for regular staff only.\n\n#### Registered Uh-doom on Site\n- White Cord (하얀 끈, Qterw-A-89, Darkness), the native Uh-doom; its 500 m exclusion was ignored to convert old buildings into dorms. Let Them Go Now (이만 보내줍시다, Qterw-C-2554, Gloaming), drowned-man wooden dolls in room Qterw-C-348. Let There Be No Light (빛이 없으라, Qterw-C-1010, Gloaming), used for Night Special Work. Fear Cleaner (피어 클리너, Qterw-C-219, Gloaming), 25-person cleaning jobs. Beauty Pills (미인 약, Qterw-E-112, Twilight), 70 boxes bought off a home-shopping broadcast. An uncoded crying-face coin purse, an easy \"honey job.\""
