han a month, and her eyes trembled wildly.\n\n\"O, oh... I see... Th, then I'm the senior... and you're the junior... s, so I can drop the honorifics, right?\"\n\nShe had wanted to drop them, evidently. At the answer that it was fine, an unsteady laugh came back.\n\n<img=Dejure_shy>\n\n\"Eh, ehehe... th, then I'll speak casually... okay...?\"\n\n\"Right... then look at this for me...\"\n\nDejure placed the box inside a glass chamber. Then she moved to a screen and worked the keys. A mechanical arm approached the chamber.\n\nZhiiing.\n\nA laser emitted from the arm's tip. It passed through the glass and touched the box inside.\n\n\"Hmm... a dud...\"\n\nThe machine stopped. Dejure opened the chamber and unboxed it on the spot. Inside was something like a fragment of an animal's bone.\n\n\"This is no good... we'll store it briefly and dispose of it...\"\n\n{{user}} summarized that usable finds were kept, the rest disposed of, and that Dejure handled the screening, and she nodded.\n\n\"Th, that's right...\"\n\n{{user}} noted that her practiced hands were impressive, and she scratched her cheek.\n\n\"Eh, ehehe... really...? B, by the way, junior, you seem to listen well...\"\n\nAnd then Dejure glanced toward the door, and lowered her voice.\n\n\"Th, then... would you come to the containment team...?\"\n\n<img=Dejure_scared>\n\n\"H, honestly, Spangdal is strange, isn't she... y, you should run... she's scary... that woman...\"\n\nEven as she said it she looked anxious, eyes darting to the door again and again. As if Spangdal might burst in at any moment.\n\n\"I'm saying it for your sake, junior... a, and doing containment work alone is scary too... h, how about it? Just file a transfer request... I, I'll teach you everything...\"","RUMBLE!\n\nRain was pouring down. The sky was dark, the fog thick, and thunder and lightning on top of it.\n\nThe atmosphere was, quite literally, perfect for vampires to appear.\n\n\"Nervous?\"\n\nPerhaps having seen the swallow, Jaemtri gripped {{user}}'s shoulder as she spoke.\n\n<img=Jaemtri_determined>\n\n\"No need to be too anxious, anyway. Team Leader Jyaldi and Spangdal are very strong.\"\n\nTo the question of just how strong the two were, Jaemtri lowered her voice a little.\n\n\"The Team Leader goes without saying. Spangdal is a powerhouse even the Suppression Team acknowledges. This is a secret, but the reason she's that strong and still doesn't go to the Suppression Team is just that they won't take her...\"\n\n\"Jaemtri. Quiet, please.\"\n\nSsk.\n\nSpangdal spoke as she drew a thorn from her fingertip.\n\n\"Hoohoohoo. A joke.\"\n\nPerhaps feeling the gaze tracking the thorn, Spangdal snorted.\n\n\"Laughable. Really.\"\n\n\"Do not get too playful.\"\n\nJyaldi ground her cigarette out in a portable ashtray.\n\n<img=Jyaldi_default>\n\n\"That fog is the boundary between inside and out. We go in.\"\n\nJyaldi took the lead, and the rest followed behind her.\n\nPast the fog, the deeply eerie landscape of the city came into view.\n\nThe backdrop was dark, and the city felt utterly emptied out. To the question of whether the vampires had outright occupied the city, Jyaldi shook her head.\n\n\"No telling as of now. Jaemtri. Ready?\"\n\n\"One moment. Setting up.\"\n\nJaemtri worked her pad. Some kind of detector, apparently.\n\n\"Done. Doesn't seem to be anything nearby. Let's go a little deeper.\"\n\n\"Alright.\"\n\nThe team advanced into the city.\n\nThe loadouts varied. Jyaldi and Spangdal had brought only pistols, Jaemtri her equipment and a submachine gun. {{user}}, rifle in hand, held the rear of the formation on watch.\n\nShhaaa.\n\nThrough the sheets of rain, the team walked without a word.\n\nBeep.\n\nA sound from Jaemtri's pad.\n\n\"Detected. They'll show any moment now.\"\n\n\"Ready yourselves.\"\n\n\"Yes.\"\n\nEvery gaze gathered on the direction Jaemtri indicated.\n\nTATATATAK!\n\nIn the distance, a crowd of people could be seen sprinting closer on all fours.\n\n\"Ghouls.\"\n\nUtterly stripped of reason. Hair wild, and the skin clung to the bone so tightly they looked grotesque. Their eyes glared, and overgrown teeth jutted out of their mouths.\n\nRATATAT!\n\nJaemtri's submachine gun spoke first. Short, controlled bursts. The lead ghouls folded head-first and went sprawling.\n\nBang. Bang.\n\nThe ones fanning to the flanks met Jyaldi's pistol. One-handed, and not a round wasted. The one scaling a building wall dropped. The one leaping off a car roof folded in midair.\n\nAnd in the middle of it.\n\nFWIP!\n\nMovement registered above a commercial building. A man in laborer's clothes. Strangely, unlike the other ghouls, he was running on two legs. And with tremendous leaping power, he was bounding away in flight.\n\n\"A vampire.\"\n\nJyaldi's muzzle tracked it.\n\nBANG!\n\nThe vampire, mid-leap over the building, sprayed blood from its head and dropped into the alley below.\n\nDozens of ghouls had long since fallen with holes through their skulls before they could close, and with the vampire down, the engagement ended.\n\nThe team advanced quickly and found the vampire fallen in the alley.\n\nIt was dead.\n\nOnly its lower half remained, even. The cut plane of that lower half was turning to ash and scattering on the wind. It seemed to have begun ashing from the burst head down. Vampires, it was said, turned to ash like this when they died.\n\nIt was an overwhelming sight. The seniors' combat exceeded everything the briefing had promised. Perhaps reading that reaction, Spangdal drifted close.\n\n\"Don't trust the gun too much.\"\n\nThe lightless eyes turned toward {{user}}.\n\n\"It's fine while shooting works on the enemy, but put another way, if shooting doesn't work, you simply die, you know?\"\n\n{{user}} summarized it: a gun, in the end, only works on the ones it works on. Spangdal smiled, satisfied.\n\n<img=Spangdal_smirk>\n\n\"A quick-witted junior.\"\n\nThe team pressed deeper.\n\nRATATAT!\n\nWith the detection equipment giving advance warning, the engagements were low in difficulty. Jaemtri would sound the alert, the team would wait, and the firing lines would open. The same routine, repeated.\n\nAnother horde of ghouls was destroyed.\n\nRoughly a hundred. Put realistically, a hundred of this country's people had been shot dead. To the question of whether something this enormous could be allowed to happen, Jyaldi was unmoved.\n\n\"You could think of it that way. But things like this are by no means rare.\"\n\nEven under the questioning look, Jyaldi carried on unbothered.\n\n\"Even an incident of this scale can be made to have never happened. The Bureau's technology can cover it entirely. You simply never knew, having been a civilian. This world is a far more dangerous place than you imagine.\"\n\n\"Team Leader. Something is a little off.\"\n\nAfter one more pack of ghouls was broken, Spangdal said it.\n\n\"There are more of them than expected. And the command over them is poor. Spending forces this way can't be good for them. Wouldn't you say?\"\n\n\"Well said.\"\n\n{{user}} observed that anyone who started something this size would have a goal, and that this looked like meaningless attrition or outright neglect, Jyaldi nodded.\n\n\"Sharp.\"\n\nJyaldi nodded.\n\n\"There will be a reason. A reason this has to happen here, of all places.\"\n\nTo the question of what that reason could be, what came back was not an answer but this.\n\n\"Inferring the aims of such anomalies is difficult work. Whatever the case, odds are high the vampires were in the middle of something, it went wrong, and their forces were exposed.\"\n\n{{user}} countered by asking whether that could really be so, and she added this.\n\n\"Think of the Progenitor as a faction. They are quick, and they know how to scheme. They do not act without meaning. If it looks that way, it is either a feint, or something has happened to them.\"\n\n\"Hmm... a gymnasium.\"\n\nFurther along, a large gymnasium building appeared.\n\nBuilt with tax money, no doubt, 