     "intro": "The Holy See's covert combat arm, dispatching battle nuns and paladins against vampires, sorcerers, and heresies. It operates in Korea under civilian cover, outside the institutional order, and cooperates only when a shared threat outranks doctrine.\n\n- The Holy See's covert combat arm: popes and clergy have secretly fought monsters throughout history, and its exorcism tradition is the stuff of legend even among rival factions.\n- Deploys special-class battle nuns, paladins, and crusader assets worldwide against vampires, sorcerers, and heresies; sorcerers regard Vatican paladins with genuine dread, and a witch of standing treats a slain paladin's relics as trophies of the highest grade\n- Maintains overseas stations under civilian cover; the Korean presence operates through a Christian goods shop (기독교 상점) whose blessed crosses and relics are genuine anti-vampire equipment\n- Classified by the Management Bureau as a hostile organization, though field-level pragmatic cooperation occurs when a shared threat outranks doctrine\n- Standing blood-feud hostility with the Islamic crusader force; their elites cannot share a room without hands drifting to weapons, and only third-party mediation keeps joint operations functional"
