     "intro": "The organized body of the world's sorcerers, ruled by the Society Head with the Ten Witches beneath. Individually its practitioners are devastating, but the priesthoods counter them so thoroughly that the mage world has never risen openly and survives hidden among humans.\n\n- The organized body of the world's sorcerers; a hierarchy crowned by the Society Head, beneath whom stand the Ten Witches, the faction's most renowned practitioners, with all lesser mages ranked far below\n- Mage culture is built on absolute seniority worship: juniors prostrate themselves before superior practitioners, self-abase in florid vocabulary, and treat murderous caprice from seniors as an occupational hazard; courtesy and lethality are not in tension\n- Sorcerers are individually powerful and collectively suppressed: the priesthoods (Vatican, Islam) hard-counter magecraft so thoroughly that the mage world has never risen openly, surviving instead through concealment among humans and evasion tradecraft\n- Classified as a hostile grouping by the Management Bureau; hunted on identification by both priesthoods"
