    "fields": {
-    "intro": "An internet board with a madhouse reputation, where a meaningful share of the lunacy is real survivor testimony. Both Bureaus monitor it, and users who post or search carelessly disappear.{{getvar::fac_extra}}\n\n##### Overview\n- An internet board nominally about world politics, but in practice one of the internet's densest concentrations of conspiracy theories: the deep state, aliens, brain parasites, rigged lotteries, and similar claims. Its public reputation is that of a gathering place for lunatics.\n- That reputation conceals the fact that a meaningful portion of its content is true. Many of its regular users are survivors of genuine anomalous encounters sharing what they witnessed.\n- The board's knowledge is fragmentary and limited to the survivor's side of events. Its users know that suited agents abduct people and that those taken never return, but they do not know who the agents are, which organization they belong to, or why they take people.\n- Genuine testimony and fabrication look almost identical on the board and are mocked equally. Even so, reports of real phenomena often appear there years before any organization acknowledges them, making the board a genuine source of early warning.",
+    "intro": "An internet board with a madhouse reputation, where a meaningful share of the lunacy is real survivor testimony. Both Bureaus monitor it, and users who post or search carelessly disappear.\n\n##### Overview\n- An internet board nominally about world politics, but in practice one of the internet's densest concentrations of conspiracy theories: the deep state, aliens, brain parasites, rigged lotteries, and similar claims. Its public reputation is that of a gathering place for lunatics.\n- That reputation conceals the fact that a meaningful portion of its content is true. Many of its regular users are survivors of genuine anomalous encounters sharing what they witnessed.\n- The board's knowledge is fragmentary and limited to the survivor's side of events. Its users know that suited agents abduct people and that those taken never return, but they do not know who the agents are, which organization they belong to, or why they take people.\n- Genuine testimony and fabrication look almost identical on the board and are mocked equally. Even so, reports of real phenomena often appear there years before any organization acknowledges them, making the board a genuine source of early warning.",
     "structure": "##### User Structure\n- Floaters are the anonymous majority: tourists, mockers, and one-time survivors who post an experience once and never mention it again.\n- Named regulars use fixed nicknames and accumulate traceable posting histories. They are either unaware of the risk or skilled at concealing themselves.\n- True regulars form the inner circle. They retain their board nicknames but communicate through a separate invitation-only hidden messenger, and every member has survived at least one genuine anomalous encounter.\n- The Sub-moderator serves as the board's visible manager. They oversee the deletion of dangerous exposure posts, represent the group in negotiations, and conceal their identity, methods, and information holdings.",
     "personnel": "##### The Survivor Collective\n- The group existed before internet forums and now uses the World Politics Forum as its public gathering place.\n- Its principle is that someone untouched by the hidden world is safest knowing nothing, while someone already exposed to it may die without information. It therefore collects information about the hidden world for survival and trades that information when necessary. Loyalty among members is genuine, and anyone who obtains survival-critical information passes it to the group."
